      "line_end": 6,
      "title": "Search term interpolated into SQL",
      "description": "The index action puts params[:q] directly into the SQL text of the where clause. Nothing escapes or binds the value. Any authenticated caller can inject SQL and read or change any table, including api tokens. The caller can also break the query. Pass the search term as a bound parameter and escape LIKE wildcards with sanitize_sql_like.",
      "suggested_change": "    users = users.where(\"email LIKE ?\", \"%#{User.sanitize_sql_like(params[:q])}%\") if params[:q].present?",
      "source": "semgrep:ruby.rails.security.injection.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The index action puts params[:q] directly into the SQL text of the where clause. Nothing escapes or binds the value.",
      "consequence": "Any authenticated caller can inject SQL and read or change any table, including api tokens. The caller can also break the query.",
      "fix": "Pass the search term as a bound parameter and escape LIKE wildcards with sanitize_sql_like."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "critical",
