      "line_end": 2,
      "title": "Destroy action skips the admin check",
      "description": "The change adds destroy to the require_admin exception list. The destroy action then deletes any user by id with no ownership or role check. Any authenticated user can delete every other user, including admins. This causes data loss. Keep destroy behind require_admin, or scope the lookup to the current user.",
      "suggested_change": "  before_action :require_admin, except: [:index, :show]",
      "source": "semgrep:ruby.rails.security.brakeman.check-unscoped-find.check-unscoped-find",
      "candidate": "c3",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The change adds destroy to the require_admin exception list. The destroy action then deletes any user by id with no ownership or role check.",
      "consequence": "Any authenticated user can delete every other user, including admins. This causes data loss.",
      "fix": "Keep destroy behind require_admin, or scope the lookup to the current user."
